_meanings:
.²1 The world, a division of the universe; (roughly speaking there are
 three {%lokas%} {#svarga, pfTvI#} and {#pAtAla#}, but according to
 fuller classification the {%lokas%} are fourteen, seven higher regions
 rising from the earth one above the other; {%<ab>i. e.</ab>%} {#BUrloka, Buvarloka#},
 {#svarloka, maharloka, janarloka, taparloka#}, and {#satyaloka#} or {#brahmaloka#};
 and seven lower regions, descending from the earth one below the other;
 {%<ab>i. e.</ab>%} {#atala, vitala, sutala, rasAtala, talAtala, mahAtala#}, and {#pAtAla#}).
.²2 The earth, terrestrial world ({#BUloka#}); {#ihaloke#} in this world
 (<ab>opp.</ab> {#paratra#}).
.²3 The human race, mankind, men, as in {#lokAtiga, lokottara#} <ab>&c.</ab> <ab>q. v.</ab>
.²4 The people or subjects (<ab>opp.</ab> the king); {#svasuKaniraBilAzaH Kidyase#}
 {#lokahetoH#} <ls>Ś. 5. 7</ls>; <ls>R. 4. 8</ls>.
.²5 A collection, group, class, company; {#AkfzwalIlAn naralokapAlAn#}
 <ls>R. 6. 1</ls>; or {#SaSAma tena kzitipAlalokaH#} <ls n="R.">7. 3</ls>.
.²6 A region, tract, district, province.
.²7 Common life, ordinary practice (of the world); {#lokavattu lIlAkEvalyam#}
 <ls>Br. Sūt. II. 1. 33</ls>; {#yaTA loke kasyacidAptEzaRasya rAjYaH#} <ab>&c.</ab> <ls>Ś. B.</ls>
 (and diverse other places of the same work).
.²8 Common or worldly usage (<ab>opp.</ab> Vedic usage or idiom); {#vedoktA vEdikAH#}
 {#SabdAH sidDA lokAcca lOkikAH, priyatadDitA dAkziRAtyA yaTA loke vede ceti#}
 {#prayoktavye yaTA lOkikavEdikezviti prayuYjate#} <ls>Mbh.</ls> (and in diverse
 other places); {#ato'smi loke vede ca praTitaH puruzottamaH#} <ls>Bg. 15. 18</ls>.
.²9 Sight, looking.
.²10 The number ‘seven’, or ‘fourteen’.
.²11 <ab>Ved.</ab> Open space; space, room.
.²12 Oneʼs own nature ({#nijasvarUpa#}); {#nazwasmftiH punarayaM pravfRIta#}
 {#lokam#} <ls>Bhāg. 3. 31. 15</ls>.
.²13 Enlightenment ({#prakASa#}); {#icCAmi kAlena na yasya viplavastasyAtmalokAvaraRasya#}
 {#mokzam#} <ls>Bhāg. 8. 3. 25</ls>.
.²14 Recompense ({#Pala#}); {#agnAveva devezu lokamicCante#} <ls>Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 15</ls>.
.²15 An object of enjoyment ({#Bogyavastu#}); {#aTo ayaM vA AtmA sarvezAM#}
 {#BUtAnAM lokaH#} <ls>Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 16</ls>.
.²16 Sight, the faculty of seeing ({#cakzurindriya#}); {#agnirlokaH#} <ls>Bṛ. Up. 3. 9. 10</ls>.
.²17 An object of sense ({#vizaya#}); {#upapattyopalabDezu lokezu ca saMmo#}
 {#Bava#} <ls>Mb. 12. 288. 11</ls>. (In compounds {#loka#} is often translated by
 ‘universally’, ‘generally’, ‘popularly’; as {#lokavijYAta#}; so {#˚vidvizwa#}).

.²1 desire for heaven; {#yA vittEzaRA sA lokEzaRoBe hyete ezaRe eva BavataH#}
 <ls>Bṛ. Up. 3. 5. 1</ls>.
.²2 desire for the good opinion of the public.

liked by the people, popular; {#Bava pituranurUpastvaM#}
 {#guRErlokakAntEH#} <ls>V. 5. 21</ls>.
.

.²1 a regent or guardian of a quarter of the world; {#lalitABinayaM tamadya#}
 {#BartA marutAM drazwumanAH salokapAlaH#} <ls>V. 2. 18</ls>; <ls>R. 2. 75</ls>, <ls n="R.">12. 89</ls>, <ls n="R.">17. 78</ls>;
 (the {%lokapālas%} are eight; see {#azwadikpAla#}).
.²2 a king, sovereign.

.²2 differing from the world, eccentric, singular; {#unmAdavannftyati lokabAhyaH#}
 <ls>Bhāg. 11. 2. 40</ls>.
.

.²1 worldly affairs, the course of worldly life, business of the world;
 {#tasmAllokayAtrArTI nityamudyatadaRqaH syAt#} <ls>Kau. A. 1. 4</ls>; <ls>Mb. 3. 150. 31</ls>;
 <ls>Dk. 2. 8</ls>; {#evaM kileyaM lokayAtrA#} <ls>Mv. 7</ls>; {#yAvadayaM saMsArastAvat#}
 {#prasidDEveyaM lokayAtrA#} <ls>Ve. 3</ls>.
.²2 a popular usage or custom; {#ezoditA lokayAtrA nityaM strIpuMsayoH#}
 {#SuBA#} <ls>Ms. 9. 25</ls>.
.²3 worldly existence, career in life; <ls>Māl. 4</ls>, <ls n="Māl.">6</ls>.
.²4 support of life, maintenance.

.²1 the way of the world, a custom prevalent in the world; {#lokavfttamanuzWeyaM#}
 {#kftaM vo bAzpamokzaRam#} <ls>Rām. 4. 25. 3</ls>.
.²2 an idle talk or gossip; {#na lokavfttaM varteta vfttihetoH kaTaMcana#} <ls>Ms. 4. 11</ls>.

.²1 having the world as a witness; in the face of the world; {#pratyakzaM#}
 {#PalamaSnanti karmaRAM lokasAkzikam#} <ls>Mb. 3. 32. 6</ls>.
.²2 attested by witnesses.
